{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s trackers’ limits on one request, 25 events and 40,000 bytes of body, and an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of up to 150,000 bytes in a request of its own."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow’s mobile trackers send at most 25 events and 40,000 bytes in a request by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and an event larger than that in a request of its own. A collector refuses a body over 2 MB","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with 413, and a request larger than its stream takes (192,000 bytes on SQS, 1 MB on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Kinesis, by default) becomes a failed event though the collector answers 200. So an event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of up to 150,000 bytes of JSON is sent alone, within the smallest of those, and a larger one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is left out as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/document